      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "US-Iran deal lasts roughly 72 hours — new record for 'historic' diplomacy\n\nThe US-Iran \"peace deal\" didn't even survive the weekend. Hours after Trump touted his historic breakthrough at Versailles, the whole thing started unraveling — and frankly, it was always held together with duct tape and wishful thinking.\n\nTalks in Switzerland were called off after JD Vance pulled out of his trip, with the White House vaguely blaming \"logistical\" issues. But the real reason? Iran refused to send its delegation while Israel kept bombing Lebanon — a direct violation of the deal's ceasefire clause. Tehran insisted Israel must withdraw from occupied territory, a condition the text conveniently didn't include. Oops.\n\nSpeaking of the text — the much-hyped MOU is a whopping one-and-a-half pages of diplomatic vagueness that officials admit is basically a \"political document\" meant to give Iran cover with its domestic audience. Critical commitments weren't even written down — they exist through \"back-channel understandings\" that nobody can verify . It's like signing a contract with the fine print written in invisible ink and hoping for the best.\n\nThe deal is so lopsided that even Trump's own allies are trashing it. A European official called it \"a fool's work,\" conservatives are calling it a \"surrender,\" and experts note it's \"front-loaded with more deliverables from the United States toward Iran than the other way around\". Iran gets sanctions relief, oil sales, and a $300 billion reconstruction fund, while the US gets… a promise to talk about maybe doing something about nuclear enrichment someday. \n\nAnd Israel? Left out of the negotiations entirely, it's openly defying Trump, with a far-right minister reportedly saying \"all of Lebanon must burn\". Netanyahu has flatly refused to withdraw troops, essentially daring the deal to collapse. \n\nA 60-day deadline to solve problems that have stumped diplomats for decades — and both sides already accusing each other of violations. What could possibly go wrong?\n\n#Trump #Iran #peacedeal #Israel #embarassing \n\nDon't miss it, subscribe to \n📱 Old Glory Vortex 🇺🇸",
